PATCH 628: preserve FILEMGR 6032's complete successful read result (board:0003).

Original 6085 INT 21h returns the resident kernel's full DWORD EAX.
6087 checks CF, 608d stores DWORD [937],EAX, and 60a3/60a8 return that
stored DWORD after closing the file. The decompile instead combines
the low AX word with an uninitialized extraout_var. Read the existing
full EAX shadow supplied by the shared resident-kernel read owner;
do not add another file loader or infer the count from the request.

The read-only original 600-ms capture reaches HIGH.DTL (2052 bytes)
and the complete DSOUNDS.BIN (134240 bytes, EAX=00020c60). All 39
frames, 27518 mixed PCM samples and the endpoint match the unprobed
capture. The parent regression invokes actual ordered-patched 6032,
5cc2 and 5d50 with the real DOS/VGA owners: native returns a garbage
high word and WASM returns only 3168 for DSOUNDS. Both already copy
the entire asset correctly. Compare full query/load counts, saved
count, file contents and untouched destination guards on both targets.

Scope is the successful read-result width. Error CF, other file-service
register contracts, sound startup/IRQ and final mixed PCM remain open.
--- a/fist_ext.c
+++ b/fist_ext.c
@@ -9255,7 +9255,7 @@
       uRam000f000c = param_4;
       uRam000f0010 = unaff_ES;
       fist_int_dispatch();
-      uVar1 = CONCAT22(extraout_var,uRam000f0000);
+      uVar1 = *(uint *)(g_mem + 0xf0020); /* 608d: DWORD EAX from the resident kernel */
       param_5 = (uint)uRam000f0008;
       param_6 = uRam000f000a;
       uVar2 = uRam000f0004;
